10	 * must carry 8 to 15 digits after the {@code '+'}.
11	 *
12	 * <p>So {@code "0412 345 678"} becomes {@code "+61412345678"} and {@code "+64 21 123 456"}
13	 * becomes {@code "+6421123456"}.
14	 *
15	 * <p>Where the country code has a known fixed national-number length, that length is enforced:
16	 * {@code +61} requires 9 national digits and {@code +1} requires 10. A number whose national
17	 * part is the wrong length for its country code is rejected. Country codes with no known rule
18	 * are constrained only by the general 8-to-15-digit bound.
19	 */
