## 2. Membership number and check digit

### `AssignMembershipNumber.java`
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java`

Format `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of registration-date year. Runs after `AssignCustomerCode` and `ApplyRegistrationDate`.
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    int yy = owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100;
    owner.setMembershipNumber(String.format("%s-M%02d", owner.getCustomerCode(), yy));
}
```

### Check digit — `Luhn.java` + `Owner.getCheckDigit()`
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Luhn.java`:
```java
public static int checkDigit(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return 0;
    }
    int sum = 0;
    boolean doubling = true;
    for (int i = value.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        char c = value.charAt(i);
        if (c < '0' || c > '9') {
            continue;
        }
        int digit = c - '0';
        if (doubling) {
            digit *= 2;
            if (digit > 9) {
                digit -= 9;
            }
        }
        sum += digit;
        doubling = !doubling;
    }
    return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
}
```

The check digit is a transient derived getter on the entity (`Owner.java`, lines 189-196), computed over the `customerCode`:
```java
@Transient
public int getCheckDigit() {
    return Luhn.checkDigit(this.customerCode);
}
```

### Registration date that feeds the `-M<YY>` segment
- `ResolveRegistrationDate.java` — resolves supplied-or-today, rolled to a business day, published as an OfficeFloor `Out<LocalDate>`.
- `BusinessDay.rollForward(LocalDate)` — weekend rolls to next Monday.
- `ApplyRegistrationDate.java` — sets it on the owner before `AssignMembershipNumber`.

